From {{inh|es|VL.|*accordāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|*accordō}}, from {{m|la|ac-}} (combining form of {{m|la|ad||to}}) + {{inh|es|la|cor||heart}}, + verb suffix {{m|la|-ō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/akoɾˈdaɾ/|[akoɾˈðaɾ]|lang=es}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb|acord|ar|pres=acuerdo}}

# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[decide]], [[arrange]]
# {{lb|es|intransitive}} to [[agree]]
#: {{ux|es|Lo '''acordaron''' por unanimidad.|t=They agreed to it unanimously.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|es|reflexive|[[acordarse]] de}} to reach agreement
# {{lb|es|reflexive|[[acordarse]] de}} to [[remember]], [[recall]]
#: {{ux|es|¿'''Se acuerda''' Ud. '''de''' esto?|t=Do you remember this?|inline=1}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[flush]], to make [[flush]], to [[level]]
# {{lb|es|transitive|music}} to [[tune]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|remember}} [[recordar]]

====Conjugation====
{{es-conj-ar|ac|rd|p=o-ue|combined=1}}

====Related terms====
